---
title: Welcome Series Blueprint (E-commerce Flow)
publishDate: '2024-04-12'
description: A complete 7-email welcome flow blueprint mapping out exact components, cadences, and conversion-optimization triggers for DTC brands.
---
Maps each welcome email to the required components from `email-components-library.md`.
Default = **7 emails**; a **5-email compression** is at the bottom. Build each email by
pasting the library's Boilerplate → the listed blocks → Footer → Close.

**Assumptions (adjust per client):** discount-led welcome (a signup incentive exists);
standard **exit on purchase**; ~11-day span. If value-led (no discount), swap the
Incentive blocks for Feature/Story blocks.

## Base template — on EVERY email
Boilerplate · **Header** (logo, linked) · **Hero** (image + hero text) · **Primary CTA**
(repeated in longer emails) · **Trust Badges** · **Footer (A or B)** · Close.
Optional **wave transitions** between light/dark sections. Preheader ≠ subject line.

---

## The 7-email default

### E1 — Welcome & Incentive  ·  trigger: immediate
Goal: welcome, deliver the signup offer, drive first purchase.
**Required:** Hero → One Column (welcome + what to expect) → **Incentive / Promo**
(signup coupon, verbatim) → Feature Section (3 core benefits) → Product Grid or
Categories Grid (entry products) → CTA → Trust Badges → Footer.
Optional: wave transitions, Secondary Copy.

### E2 — Brand Story / Founder  ·  +1–2 days, non-buyers
Goal: trust + differentiation (the "why").
**Required:** Hero → Secondary Copy or One Column (founder/brand story) → Framed
Content (mission / values / guarantee) → single CTA → Trust Badges → Footer.
Optional: Two Column (about points), signature image.

### E3 — Social Proof / Reviews  ·  +2–3 days, non-buyers
Goal: overcome skepticism with real customers.
**Required:** Hero → Section Header → **Review ×3** (with product) → Product Grid
(bestsellers) → CTA → Trust Badges → Footer.
Optional: Comparison (US vs THEM), UGC via Secondary Copy.

### E4 — Offer Reminder / Bump #1  ·  +4–5 days
Goal: urgency-driven conversion.
**Required:** Hero or Urgency Block → **Incentive / Promo** (code) → **Urgency
Countdown** → Product Grid → CTA (repeated) → Trust Badges → Footer.
**Flow filter:** opened ≥1 email in flow AND non-buyer.

### E5 — Product Education / Bestsellers  ·  +6–7 days, non-buyers
Goal: educate on the product; reduce "is it right for me?" friction.
**Required:** Hero → Single Product Feature or Multi-Product → Feature Section (icons)
→ Two Column (how it works / ingredients / specs) → CTA → Trust Badges → Footer.

### E6 — Why Us / Benefits / Rewards  ·  +8–9 days, non-buyers
Goal: deepen value + differentiate.
**Required:** Hero → **Comparison (US vs THEM)** or Feature Section → Framed Content
(guarantee / loyalty / rewards program) → Review ×1–2 → CTA → Trust Badges → Footer.

### E7 — Final Urgency / Last Chance  ·  +10–11 days
Goal: last-chance conversion before exiting the flow.
**Required:** Hero (bold) → **Incentive / Promo** (final or increased offer) →
**Urgency Countdown** → Multi-Product / Bestsellers → CTA (repeated ×2) →
Trust Badges → Footer.
**Flow filter:** opened ≥1 email in flow AND non-buyer.

